## Context

Next evidence checkpoint for the causal short paper; parent 0729, programme 0725.
The Astra/Fable discussion selected no design. Before choosing one, establish
whether past project populations can be reconstructed, not just completed-project
histories. The current 97 closed World Bank operations are discovery leads.

## First documentary acceptance check

Reconstruct one historical lender pipeline at a specified pre-intervention date.
Include an unfinished or cancelled operation and trace its membership to a dated
source. A current closed-only API list masquerading as that historical population
must fail. Record missing frames and dates rather than filling them from reports.

## Bounded actions

1. Write a scout brief using docs/jetp-scout-brief.md: one lender/instrument stratum,
   one JETP country and two provisional comparator countries; energy and an
   administratively comparable non-energy sector. Choose countries by baseline
   income/financing eligibility/energy conditions, not observed outcomes.
2. First round: at most 20 source-search/retrieval calls or 90 minutes, whichever
   comes first. Seek dated project lists, pipeline archives, financing agreements
   and evaluation reports. A subsequent round needs a named unresolved document
   or new route and an updated brief; this is not a saturation claim.
3. Test three earlier landmark populations plus a proposed exposure baseline,
   with follow-up ending before anticipation for historical checks where possible.
   Record whether membership, both stage endpoints, precision, cancellation and
   loss of visibility can be determined. Keep operation and parent-project IDs.
4. Retain the 0729 triad (mature-on-entry, pending JETP, ordinary historical case)
   as a protocol check, then audit 10–15 JETP cases only if the frame test supports
   useful expansion. Record acquisition effort and unavailable fields.

## Deliverables and exit criteria

- [ ] Frozen selection/scout brief and dated acquisition log with locators/hashes
- [ ] Frame-and-endpoint coverage matrix including missing, active and cancelled cases
- [ ] Event dates/bounds distinct from reporting and collection; no success-conditioned frame
- [ ] Evidence on comparable energy/non-energy definitions, baseline maturity and calendar coverage
- [ ] Go/narrow/defer memo for incumbent-pipeline, throughput, sector-gap and synthetic-history candidates; no effect estimate

A sparse result is acceptable. Stop at the evidence checkpoint; do not enlarge a
pool merely to improve a prospective estimate. No primary estimator is selected
here. Candidate and blocked sources remain separate from adjudicated ledger facts.

